            <ArticleTitle>The spectrum of diaphragmatic hernia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>65-6, 69-70, 73-5 passim</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diaphragmatic hernias are among the most common abnormalities of the gastrointestinal tract. Those with significant paraesophageal features may require surgical intervention to prevent potentially lethal complications. By contrast, 90% of patients with sliding hiatal hernias respond favorably to behavior modification and antisecretory drug therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
